{"title":"Career Roadmap · ASHA Supervisor","role":"ASHA Supervisor","summary":"An ASHA Supervisor supports, coordinates, mentors, and monitors Accredited Social Health Activists (ASHAs) working at the community level. The role is centered on strengthening frontline health delivery, community outreach, health awareness, referrals, reporting, and program implementation.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Community Health / Health Assistant"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Career Overview"},{"type":"p","text":"An ASHA Supervisor supports, coordinates, mentors, and monitors Accredited Social Health Activists (ASHAs) working at the community level. The role is centered on strengthening frontline health delivery, community outreach, health awareness, referrals, reporting, and program implementation."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical responsibilities can include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Supervising frontline health workers"},{"text":"Monitoring community-health activities"},{"text":"Supporting maternal and child health programs"},{"text":"Immunization follow-up"},{"text":"Community mobilization"},{"text":"Health education"},{"text":"Referral coordination"},{"text":"Data collection and reporting"},{"text":"Training and mentoring"},{"text":"Government health-program implementation"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Important qualification note","text":"“ASHA Supervisor” is not a universal standard job title with one single national eligibility pathway. ASHA supervision structures, titles, recruitment rules, and eligibility can vary by state and program. A B.Sc/BPH/allied-health qualification may support related supervisory roles, but the database should not imply that every allied-health graduate is automatically eligible for an ASHA Supervisor post."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header"