rograms","Frontline-Worker Coordination","Maternal & Child Health","Community Mobilization","Monitoring & Evaluation","Digital Health"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This pathway is particularly suitable for students interested in grassroots healthcare, community development, government health programs, NGO health initiatives, maternal-child health, and public-health program management."},{"type":"note","label":"Database note","text":"“ASHA Supervisor” should be retained as a state/program-specific target role, rather than presented as a universally guaranteed job outcome of a B.Sc/allied-health degree. For a normalized career database, useful broader titles include Community Health Supervisor, Frontline Health Worker Supervisor, Community Health Coordinator, and Public Health Program Assistant."}]}]}